name=pr-creation
version=1.2.0
description=Creating a pull request for the current feature branch. Use when: user asks to create a PR, open a PR, or make a pull request.
argument_hint=Optional: the branch name and PR title
requires=
next_step=Confirm .agents/skills.config|This skill reads ticket_prefix, branch_pattern, commit_format, base_branch, repo_owner, and repo_name from that file. Any key still on its default silently produces PRs aimed at the catalog's own repo conventions rather than this project's.|`skills.sh config show` reports repo_owner or repo_name as SOURCE=default
next_step=gh auth status|Authenticate the GitHub CLI — the skill opens the PR through `gh`, so an unauthenticated CLI fails only after the branch work is done.|`gh auth status` does not report a logged-in account
